{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Can you bind the chains of Pleiades</b> — They are stars in the north, and Kesil [Orion] in the south, and Kimah [Pleiades] binds the fruits, which are the delicacies, and Kesil the opposite; and the meaning is: Have you commanded these stars to bind and to open? The ancients said: Kimah is seven small stars, at the end of the sign of Aries, and the visible ones are six. And what seems right to me: that it is one, a large star called the left Eye of the Bull, and Kesil is a large star, the heart of the sign of Scorpio, for when these two rise in the east the aforementioned effects are seen, and this one corresponds to that one in house, in degree, and in portion."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "Resolved וכסיל הפך הדבר as 'and Kesil the opposite,' i.e., the reverse effect; the phrase is compressed and its precise scope ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:10.808295652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}